jobs.description:
**Attività principali:**

* Eseguire i test analitici di controllo qualità nell’ambito dell’area di biologia cellulare (saggi di Immunofenotipo, saggi RCL, saggi titolazione virale, saggio clonogenico, valutazione citotossicità) in osservanza alle GMP ed entro i tempi stabiliti;
* Eseguire i saggi e le analisi previsti per il trasferimento e la validazione di nuovi metodi analitici.
* Gestione del laboratorio (approvvigionamento materiali, verifica scadenze reagenti, preparazione soluzioni, verifica strumentazione);
* Fornire supporto per la redazione o revisione di documentazione (metodi analitici, SOP, etc.);
* Fornire supporto nella redazione di protocollo e report inerenti l’attività analitica eseguita.

**Requisiti:**

* Laurea in Scienze Biologiche/Biotecnologie;
* Buona conoscenza della lingua inglese;
* Esperienza pregressa in laboratorio di biologia cellulare di almeno 1 anno post laurea e analisi tramite FACS.

Salary range: 34 000 - 35 000€

**Who We Are**  
*AGC Biologics is a global Contract Development and Manufacturing Organization with a strong presence in Italy. From our Milan site, we develop and manufacture life‑changing advanced biologics for some of the world’s most innovative pharmaceutical companies. Together with our team members across Europe, the U.S., and Japan, we deliver development and manufacturing of mammalian and microbial-based therapeutic proteins, plasmid DNA (pDNA), messenger RNA (mRNA), viral vectors, and genetically engineered cells therapies. Across our global network, we are united by one mission: To work side by side with our customers in order to improve patients’ lives by bringing new biopharmaceuticals to market.*

IRCCS Ospedale San Raffaele, an internationally recognized clinical, scientific and academic institution specializing in highly complex medical conditions, is seeking Junior Laboratory Technicians to join the TIGET Clinical Lab (TCL), part of the Development Units of the San Raffaele Telethon Institute for Gene Therapy (SR-TIGET), coordinated by Dr. Matias Soncini. SR-TIGET was created in 1995 as a joint venture between Fondazione Telethon and Ospedale San Raffaele (OSR), with the mission to perform cutting-edge research on gene and cell therapy and to translate its results into therapeutic advances for genetic diseases. TCL is a Clinical Research laboratory that performs standardized analyses on samples from patients who have undergone experimental Cell and Gene Therapy. TCL is an AIFA autocertified Phase I laboratory where the biological effects of experimental Cell and Gene Therapy are studied following approved Clinical Protocols and in compliance with Good Clinical Laboratory Practice (GCLP).


Main activities

**Cellular immunology techniques:** isolation of PBMCs, immunobeads purification, flow cytometry, short-term cell culture, western blot techniques;

Molecular techniques (PCR and nucleic acid extraction, etc.);

Managing and tracking biological samples following GCLP principles;

Knowledge of English is required.


Basic Skills for the ideal candidate

Scientific Bachelor's or Master's Degree, or qualification as Biomedical Laboratory Technician;

At least one year of hands-on experience in cellular and/or molecular biology techniques;

High accuracy, reliability, and precision;

Team player, collaborative, proactive mindset.


Plus

Experience in flow cytometry;

Experience in molecular biology;

Experience in GxP laboratories;

Good oral and written English.


We offer

**Type of contract:** Co. Co. Co.;

**Strarting date:** November / December 2026;

**Duration:** 1 year, potentially renewable;

**Place of work:** SR-TIGET, Via Olgettina 58, 20132-Milan.


Applications, including a CV, can be submitted directly through the application form on this page or sent by e-mail to soncini.matias@hsr.it. Evaluation of applications and interviews will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled.


At San Raffaele Scientific Institute, a world-renowned center of excellence for clinical and scientific activities, we believe that considering diversity and promoting an open and inclusive environment is crucial to our success. We are committed to ensure that equal employment opportunities are provided and based on merit without regard to age, religion, sex, disability, medical condition, sexual orientation, cultural and social backgrounds, gender identity or expression, national or ethnic origin, or any other legally recognized status entitled to protection under applicable laws. We offer attractive conditions and rewards appropriate to an internationally competitive research organization.
